it. This PR adds a bounded observer to find how much CPU the current own-checkpoint reader spends decoding, recomputing scores, and doing the remaining checkpoint work.\n\nIt preserves all 433 scientific source files and adds a separately bound private entry, support and config. Only the archive reader's named callsite starts a timing region. Nested decode/score costs are separated without double counting, and original arguments, results, errors and aliases are restored. Saved-data checks reject incomplete or damaged records; interruptions retain partial evidence. Reports can be regenerated into a fresh folder without changing their inputs.\n\nThe first regression run caught seven draft failures. The corrected focused suite passes 136 tests, including real tiny checkpoints checked with independent terminal sums and exhaustive pure replies. The original local cohort remains in qualification history after the report-output correction.\n\nValidation: base311: 4801 passed, 65 skipped, 150 deselected in 621.86s (0:10:21); base312: 4801 passed, 65 skipped, 150 deselected in 594.09s (0:09:54); optional311: 1704 passed in 311.83s (0:05:11); optional312: 1704 passed in 252.73s (0:04:12); lint, formatting, strict typing and hooks pass. Source `899ad05`, 436-file fingerprint `81ea769018500d50c2dfcc48b0ced099d6fe424c8cff7f235540f14620da32ca`. [Both exact-source hosted jobs](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/actions/runs/43844976093) are running. Their verified receipts and the four local receipts must be published before formal collection.\n\nThe registered follow-up is one own-only observer proof, published before one complete ordinary/profiled cost-audit pair. Raw evidence must be published before analysis. No new formal measurement or Hold'em training has run at this source checkpoint; the failed budget and strength results remain unchanged. The PR stays open through the required evidence and final checks.\n\n[Prospective plan](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/issues/4#issuecomment-6910138688) · [Method](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/899ad05181bf7d2e9094bb20d1b8da84313a4f68/docs/checkpoint-replay-cpu.md) · [Learning journal, step 126](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/899ad05181bf7d2e9094bb20d1b8da84313a4f68/docs/learning-journal.md#126-check-the-tool-before-timing-checkpoint-replay)\n\nRefs #4.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-16T10:00:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T10:02:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e788184744a37d79533f9ce3395bc0fe1ac7f618","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"jimmy-sim:research/checkpoint-observer","ref":"research/checkpoint-observer","repo":{"id":1444975151,"node_id":"R_kgDOViCSLw","name":"poker-ai","full_name":"jimmy-sim/poker-ai","owner":{"login":"jimmy-sim","id":77947780,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQ3Nzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77947780?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim","html_url":"https://github.com/jimmy-sim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jimmy-sim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Personal poker AI research: simulation, CFR, reproducible Hold'em experiments, and independent solver comparison